1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
It's always deadliest before the dawn.

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Zeros and Ones is a war, thriller film directed by Abel Ferrara.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Called to Rome to stop an imminent terrorist bombing, a soldier desperately seeks news of
his imprisoned brother — a rebel with knowledge that could thwart the attack.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Navigating the capital's darkened streets, he races to a series of ominous
encounters to keep the Vatican from being blown to bits.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
JJ / Justin, played by Ethan Hawke.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Laughing Russian Agent, played by Cristina Chiriac.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Phil, played by Phil Neilson.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Luciano, played by Valerio Mastandrea.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Valeria, played by Valeria Correale.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Serious Russian Agent, played by Dounia Sichov.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Zeros and Ones is a 2021 thriller film written and directed by Abel Ferrara.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Starring Ethan Hawke, it follows an American mercenary attempting to uncover a
plot to blow up the Vatican during the COVID-19 lockdowns in Rome.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The film had its world premiere in the main competition of the 74th Locarno Film
Festival in August 12, 2021, where it won the Best Direction Award.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
It received a limited theatrical release and a simultaneous digital
release on the United States by Lionsgate on November 19, 2021.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The film explores themes of rome, italy, twin brother, terrorism, pandemic.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The tone is dark and intense.
